{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix + measurements.\n\n`monkeypatch.setenv(\"JIRA_DC_FIELD_READY_TIMEOUT\", \"0\")` in the test, plus an assertion that the stub saw exactly ONE `/rest/api/2/field` read.\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test_a_missing_epic_field_aborts_provisioning` call | **120.38s** | **<0.005s** (below the durations floor) |\n| whole test invocation | 121.21s | **0.73s** |\n\n**-120.4s of wall clock**, and it was pure idle — the CPU was asleep.\n\nWhy a zero budget is the right lever rather than merely a small one: `await_required_fields` always makes at least one attempt, then breaks on `monotonic() >= deadline` BEFORE calling `sleep`. So with budget 0 the loop is DETERMINISTIC — exactly one poll, zero sleeps — which is what makes the poll-count assertion a real guard rather than a timing heuristic. Reaching a real sleep requires another lap, and another lap necessarily produces a second field read.\n\nGuard proven live. Changing the injected budget from `0` to `3` (i.e. letting it actually sleep):\n\n    E       AssertionError: expected exactly one field poll, got 4\n    FAILED tests/unit/test_live_jira_dc_provisioning.py::test_a_missing_epic_field_aborts_provisioning\n\nReverted immediately.\n\nAmbient-environment robustness proven. Re-running with `JIRA_DC_FIELD_READY_TIMEOUT=300` already exported: **1 passed in 0.69s** — `setenv` overrides an ambient value rather than being defeated by it. This is exactly the case that would have silently broken a `FIELD_READY_BUDGET_S` monkeypatch, since `_field_ready_timeout()` prefers the env var.\n\nIsolation and production defaults: `tests/unit/test_live_jira_dc_provisioning.py`, `test_live_jira_dc_conftest.py` and `test_jira_dc_capability_map_workflow.py` run together — **58 passed in 4.36s** — so the override did not leak. `git diff --stat origin/main` for `scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.py` and `tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py` is EMPTY: `FIELD_READY_BUDGET_S` is still 120.0 and no production readiness behaviour changed.\n\nGates: 11 `check_*` scripts pass, `check_wall_clock_asserts` clean (the new assertion is a poll count, not a time budget), complexity `active=59 new=0 increased=0 stale=0`, lint and typecheck clean."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786605792536240001,"uuid":"b74fc0d7-f72a-4aac-966e-60eef1379c05"}